# README.source for linuxdevstackbox

## Toolchain requirements not declared in Build-Depends

Building this package requires a Node.js >= 20 (with npm) and a Rust
>= 1.77.2 toolchain (with cargo), in addition to the dependencies declared
in debian/control.

They are intentionally NOT listed in Build-Depends: the toolchain packages
shipped in current Debian stable releases (rustc/cargo from 1.7x on recent
releases, nodejs 18 on Ubuntu 24.04) are older than the versions the
upstream project requires and supports. Declaring them would advertise
buildability that the declared packages cannot actually provide.

Build environments (CI or local) must therefore provide these toolchains
themselves - for example rustup's stable toolchain and NodeSource or a
version manager for Node.js - and put them on PATH before running
dpkg-buildpackage. The debian/rules build invokes `npm` and `cargo` from
PATH.

## Build overview

debian/rules performs the real upstream build:

1. `npm ci` + `npm run prebuild` + `npm run build` (Vite frontend; the
   prebuild step stages the phpMyAdmin runtime into
   packaging/phpmyadmin-runtime from the vendored phpmyadmin/ source).
2. `cargo build --release --frozen` in src-tauri (the Tauri backend;
   Cargo.lock pins the dependency set).

The resulting binary, the staged phpMyAdmin runtime, the desktop entry and
the hicolor icons are installed under /usr. Runtime dependencies (Apache,
MariaDB, PHP, the WebKitGTK/GTK libraries, polkit) are declared in the
binary package stanza of debian/control.

All declared Build-Depends are satisfied by packages from the Debian/Ubuntu
archives; no package in the build depends on files outside the source tree
and the documented toolchains.
